{Eleusine carocana Gaertn., \gvdb{296--297; cf.\ 216}.  The common millet ``\emph{rāgi}.''  Normally thought of as of African origin but known in India in the early first millennium if this identification is correct.  Also called \emph{markaṭahastatṛṇa} ``monkey-hand grass'' by commentators}


