{foxtail millet}%
{also \emph{śyāmā}. Setaria italica (L.) P. Beauvois \cite[263--264]{gvdb}, \cite[576]{meul-plants1}.  The most widely-grown species of millet in Asia.  Some say Callicarpa macrophylla, Vahl. See \volcite{1}[334]{avs}, \volcite{1}[\#420]{NK}. The fruits of S. italica and C. macroyphylla are similar.  See also \cite[413]{gvdb}, where the authors suggest that \emph{priyaṅgu} is meant by \emph{gondī} or \emph{gondanī} and may have originally been called \emph{gundrabīja}}


