\bibglsnewentry{śigru}%
{sort={horseradish|tree|},
type={plants}}%
{horseradish tree}%
{Moringa oleifera Lam. See \cite[759]{IGP}, \cite[603]{meul-plants1}, \volcite{1}[396]{dymock}, \cite[398--399]{gvdb}, \volcite{1}[396--399, \#336]{imp}. The definitive study is that by \citet{meul-2009}, who suggested that the name may have denoted pungent, pro-pitta plants, while \citet{spie-2022} took this further, suggesting that "\emph{śigru}" may historically have referred more generally to plants with a sharp taste, perhaps including garlic}


