\bibglsnewentry{karaṭā}%
{sort={mountain|gardenia|},
type={plants}}%
{mountain gardenia}%
{see \egls{karaghāṭa}, as read for \emph{karaṭā} in the vulgate text of SS 5.2.5.  Not in \cite{gvdb} as such.  This poisonous root cannot at present be securely identified, although mountain gardenia has poisonous fruits.  \citet[255]{moni-sans} cite an unknown lexical source that equates \emph{karaṭa} (mn.) with safflower (\emph{Carthamus tinctorius}, L.), but this plant does not have a poisonous root either}


