    \cite[314--316, 324]{gvdb}.  One of the twenty-two drugs in the group 
    \emph{madanādi}.  \citeauthor{gvdb} and \cite[310--313]{adps}
    discuss the long controversy about the identity of this plant. 
    Sansevieria roxburghiana Schult. \& Schult.f.\ (``Indian bowstring
    hemp'') was preferred by \citet[590]{meul-plants1} and the sources he
    cited, including \volcite{1}[\#2216]{NK}, \volcite{4}[2457]{imp}; 
    \cite[310]{adps} mention this identity as being local to Bengal, but note 
    that that plant is not a creeper, as \emph{mūrvā} should be}
