It should be an aromatic in this context.  \citeauthor[371]{moni-sans} said ``two kinds of Dūrvā grass and of a kind of Cyperus'' on lexical authority, perhaps also the \emph{Rājanighaṇṭu} where it is listed amongst sweet-smelling plants. Other sources identify it as Cissus quadrangularis, L., i.e., Veltd grape \citep[272]{gupt-1887}, or \egls{bilva}}


