{This is an unidentifiable plant whose name means, etymologically, "with lilies."  \cite[292]{moni-sans} gives Nymphoides indica (L.) Kuntze (formerly Villarsia indica) on no authority; I have used the common name of N. indica as a possiblity, but this is not known to be poisonous; on the contrary, it is used medicinally \citep{khan-2018}.  N. indica is illustrated on p.\,6 of the Voynich manuscript.  \citet{khan-2018} assert that this is the same plant as \emph{tagara}, although this is not a widely-held view (see \egls{tagara})}


